{"description":"DeadLine BBS guardrail hook: whenever app code is saved, re-verify the resurrection still boots — JS parses, no network calls sneak in, and no real personal data appears in seed content. This is the hook used during the Kiroween build to keep the 'offline, fictional, zero-dependency' steering rules honest.","name":"on-save-verify","then":{"prompt":"A DeadLine BBS source file was just edited. Run these checks and report pass/fail for each, fixing nothing without asking: (1) `node --check js/app.js` passes. (2) No external network references exist in index.html, css/style.css or js/app.js — grep for 'http://', 'https://', 'fetch(', 'XMLHttpRequest' and confirm the only matches, if any, are in comments or fictional text, never in code that loads or sends data. (3) Seed messages, file listings and SysOp replies in js/app.js contain only fictional names/content — flag anything that looks like a real person's data. (4) Every main-menu section is still reachable by keyboard (arrow keys + Enter, number shortcuts 1-5).","type":"askAgent"},"version":"1.0.0","when":{"patterns":["index.html","css/style.css","js/app.js"],"type":"fileEdited"}}